# Repo-root ignore for EAS Build uploads.
#
# mobile-app/ sits inside this monorepo, and EAS builds its upload archive from
# the repository root rather than from the app folder. Without this file that
# archive came out at 424 MB — the app is ~2 MB, the rest was desktop/ (3 GB),
# backend/ (1.3 GB), frontend/ (763 MB) and dental-labs/ (388 MB) along for the
# ride. Both production builds then died mid-upload with `write EPIPE`, at
# 388/424 MB and 173/234 MB, which reads like a network fault and is really
# just an archive far too large to push reliably.
#
# Nothing here is needed to build the mobile app.
backend/
frontend/
desktop/
desktop-app/
dental-labs/
docs/
support-tool/
scripts/
.github/
.agents/
*.sh
*.md

# Dependencies and build output are restored/regenerated on the build server.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
mobile-app/ios/Pods/
mobile-app/ios/build/
mobile-app/android/build/
mobile-app/android/app/build/

# NOTE: mobile-app/ios/ itself must NOT be ignored. iOS ships as a bare build,
# so EAS uses the checked-in native project and its Podfile.lock (which pins
# hermes-engine/Pre-built). Excluding it forces a CNG prebuild with no lockfile,
# Hermes falls back to building from source, and INSTALL_PODS fails — three
# failed builds went that way before.

*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
